1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,612
This is a real web page.

2
00:00:01,612 --> 00:00:08,935
A profile card, a round photo, a button that changes color when you point at it, and three cards that stack up neatly on a phone.

3
00:00:08,935 --> 00:00:11,490
And it's made from just two small text files.

4
00:00:11,490 --> 00:00:16,600
In the next fifteen minutes, you'll build it yourself, line by line, from an empty folder.

5
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,667
No experience needed, and nothing to buy.

6
00:00:19,667 --> 00:00:23,882
You need a text editor and a web browser, and you already have a browser.

7
00:00:23,882 --> 00:00:26,826
By the end, you'll understand what every line does.

8
00:00:26,826 --> 00:00:33,351
And I'll show you the two mistakes that break almost every beginner's first page, with the real result on screen.

9
00:00:34,051 --> 00:00:35,035
Here's the plan.

10
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:37,433
First, make a folder and an empty file.

11
00:00:37,433 --> 00:00:39,893
Then write the HTML, that's the content.

12
00:00:39,893 --> 00:00:41,308
Open it in the browser.

13
00:00:41,308 --> 00:00:43,215
Then add CSS, that's the style.

14
00:00:43,215 --> 00:00:44,691
Make a button and cards.

15
00:00:44,691 --> 00:00:46,966
And finally, make it work on a phone.

16
00:00:47,666 --> 00:00:49,203
Two languages, two jobs.

17
00:00:49,203 --> 00:00:51,124
HTML says what is on the page.

18
00:00:51,124 --> 00:00:53,813
A heading, a paragraph, a picture, a link.

19
00:00:53,813 --> 00:00:55,222
CSS says how it looks.

20
00:00:55,222 --> 00:00:57,783
Colors, fonts, spacing, rounded corners.

21
00:00:57,783 --> 00:01:02,778
Think of HTML as the walls of a house, and CSS as the paint and the furniture.

22
00:01:02,778 --> 00:01:05,275
You'll keep them in two separate files.

23
00:01:05,975 --> 00:01:09,094
Make a new folder anywhere, and call it my site.

24
00:01:09,094 --> 00:01:10,719
Open a plain text editor.

25
00:01:10,719 --> 00:01:14,228
I recommend VS Code, it's free, but Notepad works too.

26
00:01:14,228 --> 00:01:18,581
Create a new file and save it inside that folder as index dot html.

27
00:01:18,581 --> 00:01:20,141
That exact name matters.

28
00:01:20,141 --> 00:01:24,885
Browsers and web servers look for index dot html first, as the home page.

29
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:27,728
One trap, especially on Windows.

30
00:01:27,728 --> 00:01:32,015
Notepad can secretly save your file as index dot html dot t x t.

31
00:01:32,015 --> 00:01:35,163
Then the browser shows your code as plain text.

32
00:01:35,163 --> 00:01:38,445
In the Save As window, set the type to All files.

33
00:01:38,445 --> 00:01:44,004
And turn on file name extensions in File Explorer, so you always see the real name.

34
00:01:44,704 --> 00:01:45,543
Now type this.

35
00:01:45,543 --> 00:01:49,978
The first line, doctype html, tells the browser this is a modern web page.

36
00:01:49,978 --> 00:01:52,076
Then the html tag wraps everything.

37
00:01:52,076 --> 00:01:58,489
Inside, the head holds information about the page, like the character set and the title on the browser tab.

38
00:01:58,489 --> 00:02:01,305
And the body holds everything you actually see.

39
00:02:01,305 --> 00:02:04,062
A big heading with h1, and a paragraph with p.

40
00:02:04,762 --> 00:02:05,905
Notice the pattern.

41
00:02:05,905 --> 00:02:07,890
Almost every tag comes in a pair.

42
00:02:07,890 --> 00:02:11,860
An opening tag, like h1, and a closing tag with a slash, slash h1.

43
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:13,485
The text goes between them.

44
00:02:13,485 --> 00:02:15,831
The pair together is called an element.

45
00:02:15,831 --> 00:02:19,620
And elements go inside other elements, like boxes inside boxes.

46
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:23,651
That's why I indent them, so you can see which box is inside which.

47
00:02:24,351 --> 00:02:25,147
Save the file.

48
00:02:25,147 --> 00:02:28,275
Then go to your folder and double click index dot html.

49
00:02:28,275 --> 00:02:29,697
It opens in your browser.

50
00:02:29,697 --> 00:02:30,606
Look at the tab.

51
00:02:30,606 --> 00:02:32,824
It says Sam Rivera, from the title tag.

52
00:02:32,824 --> 00:02:35,497
And on the page, the heading and the paragraph.

53
00:02:35,497 --> 00:02:38,568
No styling yet, just the browser's plain default look.

54
00:02:38,568 --> 00:02:39,364
That's normal.

55
00:02:39,364 --> 00:02:40,786
You just made a web page.

56
00:02:41,486 --> 00:02:42,772
Let's add more content.

57
00:02:42,772 --> 00:02:45,958
Below the paragraph, an h2, a smaller heading, What I do.

58
00:02:45,958 --> 00:02:49,145
Then u l, an unordered list, with three l i items inside.

59
00:02:49,145 --> 00:02:49,760
And a link.

60
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:52,108
The a tag, with an attribute called h ref.

61
00:02:52,108 --> 00:02:53,617
That's where the link goes.

62
00:02:53,617 --> 00:02:54,903
Here it opens an email.

63
00:02:54,903 --> 00:02:59,152
Save with Control S, or Command S on a Mac, and refresh the browser with F5.

64
00:02:59,152 --> 00:03:01,164
There's the list, and the blue link.

65
00:03:01,864 --> 00:03:04,828
This is your work loop for the rest of the video.

66
00:03:04,828 --> 00:03:07,429
Change the file, save, refresh the browser.

67
00:03:07,429 --> 00:03:08,094
Every time.

68
00:03:08,094 --> 00:03:14,566
If something doesn't change on screen, nine times out of ten you just forgot to save, or forgot to refresh.

69
00:03:15,266 --> 00:03:16,377
Now the final HTML.

70
00:03:16,377 --> 00:03:19,768
We wrap the top part in a header with a class called hero.

71
00:03:19,768 --> 00:03:22,458
A class is a name we'll use later, in the CSS.

72
00:03:22,458 --> 00:03:24,445
We add a picture with the img tag.

73
00:03:24,445 --> 00:03:29,357
Src is the file name, and alt describes the picture for people using screen readers.

74
00:03:29,357 --> 00:03:31,169
The link gets the class button.

75
00:03:31,169 --> 00:03:34,560
And the list becomes three divs, each with the class card.

76
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:39,982
Refresh, and, honestly, it looks the same as before, plus a square picture.

77
00:03:39,982 --> 00:03:40,989
That's expected.

78
00:03:40,989 --> 00:03:43,507
Classes don't do anything by themselves.

79
00:03:43,507 --> 00:03:44,767
They're just labels.

80
00:03:44,767 --> 00:03:48,670
The magic happens when CSS finds those labels and styles them.

81
00:03:48,670 --> 00:03:50,181
So let's write some CSS.

82
00:03:50,881 --> 00:03:51,532
Two steps.

83
00:03:51,532 --> 00:03:54,590
First, in the head of the HTML, this link line.

84
00:03:54,590 --> 00:03:57,845
Rel equals stylesheet, h ref equals style dot css.

85
00:03:57,845 --> 00:04:00,838
It tells the browser where your style file is.

86
00:04:00,838 --> 00:04:07,151
Second, create a new file called style dot css, in the same folder, right next to index dot html.

87
00:04:07,151 --> 00:04:10,665
Those two names must match exactly, letter for letter.

88
00:04:11,365 --> 00:04:13,608
Every CSS rule has the same shape.

89
00:04:13,608 --> 00:04:16,048
A selector, which says what to style.

90
00:04:16,048 --> 00:04:17,368
Then curly brackets.

91
00:04:17,368 --> 00:04:20,138
Inside, property, colon, value, semicolon.

92
00:04:20,138 --> 00:04:20,995
One per line.

93
00:04:20,995 --> 00:04:27,063
So body, open curly bracket, background colon, a color code, semicolon, close curly bracket.

94
00:04:27,063 --> 00:04:28,910
That's all of CSS, repeated.

95
00:04:29,610 --> 00:04:32,292
Our first rule styles the body, the whole page.

96
00:04:32,292 --> 00:04:33,433
A clean font, Arial.

97
00:04:33,433 --> 00:04:34,802
A warm background color.

98
00:04:34,802 --> 00:04:35,372
Dark text.

99
00:04:35,372 --> 00:04:38,738
Then max width, eight hundred pixels, and margin zero auto.

100
00:04:38,738 --> 00:04:43,816
Together, those two keep the page in a neat column, centered in the middle of the screen.

101
00:04:43,816 --> 00:04:45,927
And padding adds some breathing room.

102
00:04:45,927 --> 00:04:46,726
Save, refresh.

103
00:04:46,726 --> 00:04:47,581
Already better.

104
00:04:48,281 --> 00:04:49,988
Now we use the class names.

105
00:04:49,988 --> 00:04:52,705
To select a class in CSS, start with a dot.

106
00:04:52,705 --> 00:04:53,273
Dot hero.

107
00:04:53,273 --> 00:04:59,213
White background, rounded corners with border radius, padding inside, and everything centered.

108
00:04:59,213 --> 00:05:03,320
Then dot hero space img, which means only images inside the hero.

109
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:07,554
Border radius fifty percent turns the square picture into a circle.

110
00:05:08,254 --> 00:05:09,194
Next, the button.

111
00:05:09,194 --> 00:05:12,292
Remember, it's really just a link with the class button.

112
00:05:12,292 --> 00:05:15,223
Display inline block lets it have padding like a box.

113
00:05:15,223 --> 00:05:22,468
An orange background, white text, padding, a huge border radius for the pill shape, and text decoration none removes the underline.

114
00:05:22,468 --> 00:05:24,017
Then dot button colon hover.

115
00:05:24,017 --> 00:05:26,727
That's the style only while the mouse is over it.

116
00:05:26,727 --> 00:05:27,612
A darker orange.

117
00:05:28,312 --> 00:05:30,003
Here's the hover, for real.

118
00:05:30,003 --> 00:05:32,759
When I point at the button, it turns darker.

119
00:05:32,759 --> 00:05:35,201
No JavaScript, just one small CSS rule.

120
00:05:35,201 --> 00:05:40,588
That tiny change makes a page feel alive, and it tells people this thing is clickable.

121
00:05:41,287 --> 00:05:42,120
Now the cards.

122
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:44,378
Dot cards is the box around all three.

123
00:05:44,378 --> 00:05:48,004
Display flex puts the boxes inside it side by side, in a row.

124
00:05:48,004 --> 00:05:50,204
Gap adds sixteen pixels between them.

125
00:05:50,204 --> 00:05:57,337
Then each dot card gets flex one, so they share the width equally, plus a white background, rounded corners and padding.

126
00:05:57,337 --> 00:06:00,368
Save, refresh, and there's the page from the start.

127
00:06:01,068 --> 00:06:02,871
Flexbox is worth remembering.

128
00:06:02,871 --> 00:06:06,975
Display flex on the parent box, and its children line up in a row.

129
00:06:06,975 --> 00:06:10,519
Flex one on each child, and they share the space equally.

130
00:06:10,519 --> 00:06:12,509
Gap sets the space between them.

131
00:06:12,509 --> 00:06:16,799
That one idea builds menus, toolbars and card grids all over the web.

132
00:06:17,499 --> 00:06:18,210
Now, phones.

133
00:06:18,210 --> 00:06:20,580
Here's the same page on a narrow screen.

134
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:23,364
The three cards are squeezed into tiny columns.

135
00:06:23,364 --> 00:06:24,727
Ugly, and hard to read.

136
00:06:24,727 --> 00:06:25,319
Two fixes.

137
00:06:25,319 --> 00:06:32,783
First, the viewport line in the head, which tells phones to use their real screen width instead of pretending to be a desktop.

138
00:06:33,483 --> 00:06:34,790
Second, a media query.

139
00:06:34,790 --> 00:06:42,571
At max width six hundred pixels, which means on screens six hundred pixels wide or less, the cards switch to flex direction column.

140
00:06:42,571 --> 00:06:44,472
They stack, one under the other.

141
00:06:44,472 --> 00:06:48,214
Save, refresh, and now it looks like it was made for the phone.

142
00:06:48,214 --> 00:06:50,174
On a big screen, nothing changes.

143
00:06:50,874 --> 00:06:52,886
Now the two mistakes I promised.

144
00:06:52,886 --> 00:06:53,640
Mistake one.

145
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:57,600
Your CSS is ignored completely, and the page looks plain again.

146
00:06:57,600 --> 00:07:02,881
Here, the link says styles dot css, with an s, but the file is called style dot css.

147
00:07:02,881 --> 00:07:03,572
One letter.

148
00:07:03,572 --> 00:07:08,161
The browser can't find the file, so it silently skips all of your styles.

149
00:07:08,161 --> 00:07:09,229
No error message.

150
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:10,577
Mistake two.

151
00:07:10,577 --> 00:07:13,434
Half of your styles work, and the rest are just gone.

152
00:07:13,434 --> 00:07:17,370
Here, one closing curly bracket is missing, after the round picture rule.

153
00:07:17,370 --> 00:07:20,498
Now the picture is still a circle, but look at the button.

154
00:07:20,498 --> 00:07:22,062
It's a plain blue link again.

155
00:07:22,062 --> 00:07:26,591
The browser thinks the button rule is inside the broken rule, and it throws it away.

156
00:07:26,591 --> 00:07:28,370
Always close every curly bracket.

157
00:07:29,070 --> 00:07:30,487
Three more you'll meet.

158
00:07:30,487 --> 00:07:34,059
Text in the wrong place, because a closing tag is missing.

159
00:07:34,059 --> 00:07:38,679
A broken picture icon, because the image file name or folder doesn't match.

160
00:07:38,679 --> 00:07:43,052
And changes that don't show up, because you forgot to save, or refresh.

161
00:07:43,752 --> 00:07:44,192
Pro tip.

162
00:07:44,192 --> 00:07:47,108
Right click anything on your page and choose Inspect.

163
00:07:47,108 --> 00:07:50,575
Or press F12, or Control Shift I, or Command Option I on a Mac.

164
00:07:50,575 --> 00:07:53,656
These are the developer tools, built into every browser.

165
00:07:53,656 --> 00:07:57,287
Click an element, and you see exactly which CSS rules apply to it.

166
00:07:57,287 --> 00:08:00,918
You can even change a color right there, and watch it update live.

167
00:08:00,918 --> 00:08:03,174
When you like it, copy it into your file.

168
00:08:03,874 --> 00:08:04,634
Quick recap.

169
00:08:04,634 --> 00:08:07,039
HTML is the content, CSS is the looks.

170
00:08:07,039 --> 00:08:09,634
Every page starts with the same skeleton.

171
00:08:09,634 --> 00:08:10,837
Tags come in pairs.

172
00:08:10,837 --> 00:08:14,128
Classes are labels, and CSS selects them with a dot.

173
00:08:14,128 --> 00:08:15,901
Flexbox puts boxes in a row.

174
00:08:15,901 --> 00:08:17,610
A media query fixes phones.

175
00:08:17,610 --> 00:08:19,888
And edit, save, refresh, every time.

176
00:08:19,888 --> 00:08:22,294
Pause and screenshot this cheat sheet.

177
00:08:22,993 --> 00:08:25,682
Your page lives on your computer for now.

178
00:08:25,682 --> 00:08:32,893
Next on Shortcut Lab, we go back to Python, and pull the text and the tables out of P D F files automatically.

179
00:08:32,893 --> 00:08:34,992
Subscribe, so you don't miss it.
